gnificance":"routine","status":null,"text":"From committee: That the Senate amendments be concurred in, but first be re-referred to Com. on APPR. (Ayes 6. Noes 2.) (August 30). Re-referred to Com. on APPR."},{"classificationRule":"ca-committee","date":"2026-08-30","eventType":"committee_action","historyId":"119134290","location":"Assembly","sequence":26,"significance":"routine","status":null,"text":"From committee: That the Senate amendments be concurred in. (Ayes 9. Noes 1.) (August 30)."},{"classificationRule":"ca-concurred","date":"2026-08-30","eventType":"concurred","historyId":"119134291","location":"Assembly","sequence":26,"significance":"major","status":null,"text":"Urgency clause adopted. Senate amendments concurred in. To Engrossing and Enrolling. (Ayes 59. Noes 18. Page 6899.)."},{"classificationRule":"ca-enrolled","date":"2026-09-09","eventType":"enrolled","historyId":"119134292","location":"Governor","sequence":27,"significance":"major","status":null,"text":"Enrolled and presented to the Governor at 1 p.m."},{"classificationRule":"ca-approved","date":"2026-09-19","eventType":"approved_by_governor","historyId":"119134293","location":"Governor","sequence":28,"significance":"major","status":null,"text":"Approved by the Governor."},{"classificationRule":"ca-chaptered","date":"2026-09-19","eventType":"chaptered","historyId":"119134294","location":"Secretary of State","sequence":29,"significance":"major","status":null,"text":"Chaptered by Secretary of State - Chapter 330, Statutes of 2026."}],"affectedStatutes":[{"action":"IS_ADDED","code":"ELEC","text":"Section 18579 is added to the Elections Code, immediately following Section 18578, to read:"}],"approvedDate":"2026-09-19","chapter":{"citation":"Chapter 330, Statutes of 2026","number":"330","type":"CHP","year":"2026"},"chapteredDate":"2026-09-19","conditions":[],"contentHash":"f06b63159460104925c4feeff14a304a48972a2283ba26325e384b184274e417","digest":"Under existing law, a county elections official is required to prepare a certified statement of the results of an election and submit it to the county board of supervisors within 30 days of the election.\n\nThis bill would make it a felony, punishable by imprisonment for 16 months or 2 or 3 years, to seize or cause or assist in the seizure of ballots, election records, or certified voting technology before election results are certified by the elections official. The bill would also make it a felony punishable by imprisonment for 2, 3, or 4 years for any person with authority to direct another person subject to their supervision or authority to seize ballots, election records, or certified voting technology before election results are certified. By creating new crimes, this bill would impose a state-mandated local program.\n\nThe California Constitution requires the state to reimburse local agencies and school districts for certain costs mandated by the state. Statutory provisions establish procedures for making that reimbursement.\n\nThis bill would provide that no reimbursement is required by this act for a specified reason.\n\nThis bill would declare that it is to take effect immediately as an urgency statute.","effective":{"basis":"immediate_effect_flag","date":"2026-09-19","note":"The official bill data flags this measure as taking immediate effect. The date shown is the day it was chaptered by the Secretary of State; individual provisions may state other operative dates."},"expiryClauses":[],"firstObservedAt":"2026-11-20T01:12:59Z","id":"ca-20252026-ab282","identifier":"AB 282","indicators":{"Appropriation":"NO","BudgetBill":"NO","Election":"NO","FiscalCommittee":"YES","ImmediateEffect":"YES","LocalProgram":"YES","TaxLevy":"NO","Urgency":"YES","UsualCurrentExpenses":"NO","VoteRequired":"TWO_THIRDS"},"introducedDate":"2025-01-22","issueTags":[{"matchCount":null,"matchedField":"official subject line","matchedText":"Elections: seizure of election materials.","ruleId":"tag-admin-2","tag":"election-administration"},{"mat